 ------
 Maven Aar Plugin: configuration examples
 ------
 Jochen Wiedmann 
 <jochen.wiedmann@gmail.com>
 ------

Goals

  The Aar plugin allows the packaging of an Axis 2 service aar in 3 different modes,
  and the deployment of the result:

   * aar (default): generates the aar artifact

   * inplace: package the aar in the source tree

   * exploded : package an exploded aar application

   * deployaar : deploy the aar to a running Axis2 server through its administration
     console (parameters axis2AdminConsoleURL, default
     http://localhost:8080/axis2/axis2-admin, axis2AdminUser and axis2AdminPassword)

  Each mode is materialized by a goal. The plugin's goal prefix is axis2, which it
  shares with the other Axis2 plugins (the Mar plugin has goals with the same names),
  so invoke the goals with the full plugin coordinates. For instance, to generate an
  exploded aar from the current project, one would type

+--------
  mvn org.apache.axis2:axis2-aar-maven-plugin:exploded
+---------
